.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KPKG 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kpkg
.Nd one package command for every distribution kldload installs, with a snapshot first
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm install | remove
.Ar package ...
.Nm
.Cm update | upgrade
.Nm
.Cm search
.Ar term
.Nm
.Cm list | info
.Op Ar package
.Nm
.Cm help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
kldload installs Fedora, the Enterprise Linux family, Debian, Ubuntu and
Arch.
.Nm
takes the same words on all of them and runs the distribution's own tool:
.Xr pacman 8 ,
.Xr dnf 8
or
.Xr apt-get 8 ,
whichever it finds first, in that order.
.Pp
Before
.Cm install ,
.Cm remove
and
.Cm upgrade
it snapshots the running boot environment,
.Ar root Ns Pa @kpkg- Ns Ar YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS ,
and keeps the newest ten, so a transaction that breaks the machine can be
undone with
.Xr kldload-rollback 8 .
On a kldload install
.Ql dnf
and
.Ql apt
are kldload's wrapper, which takes that snapshot itself; then
.Nm
takes none, to avoid a second copy of each.
.Pp
Changing packages runs through
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm install Ar package ...
Install, without asking.
.It Cm remove Ar package ...
Remove, without asking.
.It Cm update
Refresh the package lists.
.It Cm upgrade
Upgrade everything, without asking
.Pq Ql apt-get dist-upgrade
on Debian and Ubuntu).
.It Cm search Ar term
.It Cm list Op Ar package
Installed packages, or those named.
.It Cm info Ar package
.It Cm help , Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The package manager's own; 2 for an unknown command; 1 when no package
manager is found.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kpkg list bash
bash-5.3.9-3.fc44.x86_64
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
Adding and taking away a package; not run for this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kpkg install htop
$ kpkg remove htop
# each: a snapshot of the running root, then dnf, apt-get or pacman
.Ed
.Pp
A typo:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kpkg frob
kpkg: unknown command: frob
kpkg — universal package manager (auto-detects apt/dnf/pacman)
\&...
# (exited 2)
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "kpkg: WARNING: no snapshot of ROOT was taken; the transaction goes ahead without one"
The snapshot failed (the reason is above); the change is not undoable by
rollback.
.It "No package manager found"
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr apt-get 8 ,
.Xr dnf 8 ,
.Xr kldload-rollback 8 ,
.Xr ksnap 8 ,
.Xr pacman 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-15 each transaction left two snapshots, this tool's and the
wrapper's; it takes none when the wrapper will.
On 2026-09-26 its snapshots were found never pruned.
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: the snapshot ran without
.Xr sudo 8
and any failure was discarded, so run as a user it took none and the
transaction went ahead; and an unknown command printed the usage and
exited 0.
Testing it on a Fedora 44 desktop also showed the NVIDIA container
repository kldload wrote could never load there, which was fixed in the
installer.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
.Cm update
on Fedora and Enterprise Linux is
.Ql dnf check-update ,
which lists what would be upgraded.
.Pp
Only the running boot environment is snapshotted; a package that writes
to
.Pa /home
or
.Pa /srv
is not undone by rolling back.
